      "current": {
        "id": 21821,
        "is_similar": false,
        "description": "<p>This is an open-label, pilot study evaluating the safety and preliminary efficacy of Cowpea Mosaic Virus (CPMV) administered as an intratumoral injection in dogs with mast cell tumor, soft tissue sarcoma, melanoma, and thyroid tumors. CPMV will be administered as an injection into the tumor once weekly for 4 weeks. If there is &gt;/= 25% reduction in tumor size, an additional 4 doses may be administered for a total of 8 doses. Dogs may have their tumors removed at the end of the initial 4 treatments or after 8 treatments. Hepatic and renal function tests will be monitored on the first day, at day 7 and 2,4, 6, and 8 weeks post starting treatment. Dogs will also undergo weekly physical examinations for any physical changes while on study. The tumor will undergo a biopsy before treatment, at day 14, and surgical resection will be considered at the end of study.</p>",
        "absolute_url": "https://veterinaryclinicaltrials.org/s/evaluation-of-intratumoral-cowpea-mosaic-virus-in-dogs-with-solid-tumors-613931/?ref=gallery",
