      "current": {
        "id": 21836,
        "is_similar": false,
        "description": "<p><span>This is an open-label, pilot study evaluating the safety and preliminary efficacy of radiation therapy combined with histotripsy in dogs with soft tissue sarcoma. R</span>adiation therapy will be delivered at once a week for 3 weeks and will be combined with histotripsy delivered twice a week performed 24-72 hours after radiation therapy, applied to the primary tumor using a clinical-grade histotripsy system and image guided targeting (ultrasound)<span>. Dogs may have their tumors removed at the end the study. Hepatic and renal function tests will be monitored on the first day and every other week along with physical examinations and owner interviews. The tumor will undergo a biopsy before treatment, and every other week to evaluate changes in the tumor microenvironment. This study is approved by the UT Southwestern Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee.</span></p><p><br></p>",
